data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1299,"item_id":"fc_059f54b643ecec1d016adb50711740819185fd4872d63cb108","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"inference\":\"R003\",\"packet_sha256\":\"bf019cab71c966e54b5e4231a8143057389fa0c8377bb2015aa4a604ec3c0c8f\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Fresh packet-only mathematical replay in this context: the only mathematical task material read was packet.json, in full, together with the declared Yui Audit A, self-containment, format, and logical-rules instructions. I treat N001 and the other listed inputs as allowed conditional premises and do not assess their source fidelity. The first unsupported implication in S001 is that smoothness/continuity implies the strong measurability required by M006. Continuity gives Borel measurability, but strong measurability (as required by the source contract) requires an additional measurability-to-strong-measurability result or a local proof; neither is among the listed inputs or the narrowly stated calculation policy. Thus the M006 application is not established, and N002 is not proved by this packet. I do not repair the proof. No carrier identity, canonical hash binding, or transmitted-material readback is asserted here; those checks are outside this mathematical review.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The listed inference inputs are the propositions made available in this packet and are treated as conditional premises as instructed. The stated bindings for the substantive applications are generally identifiable; this judgment does not verify source fidelity.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inputs\",\"/inference/applications\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"First gap: S001 says smoothness implies strong measurability, and the M006 checklist repeats this as continuity-based strong measurability. Continuity gives Borel measurability, but does not by itself prove the strong measurability obligation stated in M006. No permitted local derivation or input supplies that implication. Consequently M006 cannot be applied as claimed.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inputs/2/source_contract/hypotheses\",\"/inference/applications/1/hypothesis_checks\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The strong-measurability premise is a factual theorem use not accounted for by a direct input or local proof. The calculation policy is only finite-dimensional differentiation and inner-product identities; it cannot import this analysis result.\",\"locations\":[\"/logic/calculations\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/applications/1/hypothesis_checks\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The claimed differentiability conclusion and derivative formula are the stated output of M006 only if all its premises hold. The strong-measurability premise is unproved, so the complete output N002 is not established.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/2/source_contract/signature\",\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The arbitrary positive r is introduced and the final sentence generalizes from it. The H003 compact-set choice is scoped to the selected interval, and no private witness is exported in the output.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/0\",\"/inference/locals/2\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/output/statement\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"M006's required a.e. strong measurability of F near r and of F′ at r is asserted from continuity, without a proof of strong measurability. The other listed M applications have stated bindings and hypothesis checks, but this failure blocks M006.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/2/source_contract/hypotheses\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"N002 spells out its integrability, interval, support/vanishing, continuity, and measure claims rather than relying on a source theorem name or equation number. The target content is intelligible from this packet.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/definitions/0/definition\",\"/definitions/1/definition\",\"/definitions/2/definition\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The objects used in the argument are principally parameters, definitions, input binders, and recorded local declarations. The witness K is presented as a boundedness witness based on M019, and the selected interval and compact set are introduced before use. No separate undeclared-object defect precedes the mathematical gap identified above.\",\"locations\":[\"/parameters\",\"/definitions\",\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Actual dependency on strong measurability is not discharged by the cited input propositions or an earlier local fact. S001's appeal to smoothness/continuity does not establish M006's strong-measurability obligations under the packet's closed-proof standard.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/applications/1/hypothesis_checks\",\"/inputs/2/source_contract/hypotheses\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The mathematical sufficiency judgment is based only on this full packet and the declared Yui rules; no source proof, other inference body, old audit, or prefilled verdict was used. On that boundary, R003 fails at the continuity-to-strong-measurability step. This response does not claim carrier authentication, canonical hash binding, or transmitted-material readback, which are explicitly outside this mathematical review.\",\"locations\":[\"/warning\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/applications/1/hypothesis_checks\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"premises\":\"The maps used as F and Fprime are asserted to be continuous by smoothness; M006 requires a.e. strong measurability of F near r and of Fprime at r.\",\"conclusion\":\"The M006 strong-measurability hypotheses hold.\",\"judgment\":\"Unsupported: continuity/Borel measurability is not itself a proof of strong measurability under the packet's allowed premises and calculation policy. This is the first unsupported implication and blocks M006 and the output.\"}]}}"}

